# 📖 Concept 2: Variables

Imagine you have a water bottle.

You pour water into it.

Later you empty it and pour juice into it.

The bottle is still the same.

Only the contents change.

A **variable** works the same way.

It stores a value.

---

## 💻 Example 1

```python
name = "Ragesh"

print(name)
```

Output

```
Ragesh
```

---

### Understanding Every Line

```python
name
```

This is the variable name.

---

```python
=
```

This means:

> Store the value on the right inside the variable on the left.

It is called the **assignment operator**.

---

```python
"Ragesh"
```

This is the value.

---

### Visual Representation

```
name
┌─────────────┐
│  Ragesh     │
└─────────────┘
```

---

## Example 2

```python
city = "Chennai"

print(city)
```

Output

```
Chennai
```

---

## Example 3

```python
game = "Free Fire"

print(game)
```

Output

```
Free Fire
```

---

## Changing Variable Values

```python
score = 10

print(score)

score = 50

print(score)
```

Output

```
10
50
```

The value changed.

